{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/96551-can-things-escape-from-the-hedge","id":96551,"title":"Can things escape from the hedge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-22T14:48:42-07:00","id":96551,"title":"Can things escape from the hedge?","content":"I'm writing a Changeling one-shot and I want to lengthen my second act (I use 3 acts as I have about 2.5 hours normally). In the act our heroes are hiding in a Galveston beach house as a category 5 hurricane pummels the city. I think it might be cool to have things escape from the hedge during the storm and attack them. I read something about a hurricane being used as a Fae front in the core-book but I want the storm to be real and a bunch of hobgoblin's just happen to escape from the hedge due to all the destruction. Does that sound feasible or should I use some other method to make them fight (maybe they try to ride it out in the hedge? What would happen to the hedge if there was a storm in the outside world?) <br /> <br /> Thanks for any help you can give me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T15:14:38-07:00","id":96556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inspectorjavert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/96551-can-things-escape-from-the-hedge#post96551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read something about a hurricane being used as a Fae front in the core-book but I want the storm to be real</div> </div> </div> </div>The storm <i>was</i> real. Its <i>provenance</i> is what was under suspicion. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Popular changeling lore asserts that the \u201cBig Blow\u201d was, if not caused by, then certainly influenced by the Others, who rode the shrieking winds on maddened steeds and snatched up hundreds of unfortunates to be borne away to Faerie. Scattered records, mostly in the form of journals and letters written by artists, poets and other \u201csensitives\u201d report gargantuan figures dancing in the storm winds or galloping horsemen in the chaotic whirl of debris. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and a bunch of hobgoblin's just happen to escape from the hedge due to all the destruction. Does that sound feasible or should I use some other method to make them fight (maybe they try to ride it out in the hedge? </div> </div> </div>The Hedge seems to mostly stick to its own concerns as far as the natives operate, but no small number of mercenary hobs might exist, or there could be a few Hedge gates keyed to severe weather that some fae brigands make their homes near.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would happen to the hedge if there was a storm in the outside world?) </div> </div> </div>The Hedge is mostly weather-locked by region, as I understand it, but that could be a function of deeper portions - timing entry into the Hedge with a severe storm could probably result in similarly inclement weather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T15:25:37-07:00","id":97079,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of different kinds of Hobgoblin in official material (Bunyips, Border Reavers, those weird old men with the long fingers I can never remember the name of) that are specifically built around the concept of leaving the Hedge on various kinds of nefarious business. Well, the Border Reavers less so since their curse, but they have a long history of attempting it.<br /> <br /> So the answer is yes. Many Hobgoblins do slip out of the Hedge on a regular basis, and may have the same ability to enter/leave the Hedge as freely as Changelings. And as Satchel says, a Hedge Gate can be keyed to just about anything, and the presence of a hurricane could certainly work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T03:05:56-07:00","id":97420,"title":"","content":"I've got a feeling that a large part of a Goblin Chronicle book will be based on stuff escaping the hedge. If Goblins are supposed to be as important as Strix, Idigam and Fallen World in the other Chronicle Books they need to become way more important than they're now. Letting them go out of hedge is probably the simpliest way to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1969-alexander","name":"Alexander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1969_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}